s. Not an authenticated transcription: check the PDF pages.\n\n=== PDF page 1 of 34 ===\nv/VfTED ^\nWashington , Thursday , August 6, 1942\nThe President\nEXECUTIVE ORDER 9213\nExtending  the  E xistence  of the  Q uetico - \nS uperior  C ommittee\nBy virtue of the authority vested in me \nas President of the United States, I here­\nby extend the existence of the Quetico- \nSuperior Committee, created by Executive \nOrder No. 6783 of June 30, 1934, for a \nperiod of four years, from June 30, 1942, \nto June 30, 1946.\nThis order shall be effective as of June \n30, 1942.\nF ranklin  D R oosevelt \nT he W hite  H ouse ,\nAugust 4,1942.\n[F. R. Doc. 42-7565; Filed, August 4, 1942;  \n3:06 p. m.j\nRegulations\nTITLE 2 9 — LABOR\nChapter IV—United States Children’ s \nBureau\n[Amendment to Child Labor Reg. 3]\nP art 441—Employment  of M inors  B e ­\ntween  14 and 16 Years of A ge\nEMPLOYMENT OF MINORS IN THE FRUIT­\nDRYING INDUSTRY\nAugust  4, 1942.\nWhereas, the Chief of the Children’ s \nBureau, United States Department of \nLabor, issued Child Labor Regulation \nNo. 3 (Part 441, Chapter IV, Title 29, \nCode of F","path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/texts/EO_9213.txt","sha256":"c89df1250f9da49ea71f069411231bdbf39aba06455dd4062ec0a74b9e5eb180","source":{"line":236,"path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"db1b000901e5a87fdfa0c8b1559642f2633dfed6cc6d8c869068e758dc622101"}}]}
